{#- One home for the board's octopus, because the page renders it on load and the pushed board replaces it, so the first review takes the waiting one away and an idle board gets the asleep one without a reload. It sits in the head beside the title, because the board has no empty block of its own and a second one would add a second title and action (#2067, #2658). -#}
{%- set pose = board.mascot -%}
{%- if pose is not null -%}
<span class="head-character" id="board-octopus">{{ include('dashboard/components/character.html.twig', {character: pose, size: 144}, with_context = false) }}</span>
{%- else -%}
{#- An empty hidden target stays, so a board that becomes empty again gets its octopus back on the next push (#2437); it has no head-character class, so the head's flex rules leave no gap for it. -#}
<span id="board-octopus" hidden></span>
{%- endif -%}
